{"uid":"90080e85293f6a48","name":"test_the_clause_count_rewrite_folds_rather_than_deleting_a_clause","fullName":"tests.test_legal_rewrite_reprompt#test_the_clause_count_rewrite_folds_rather_than_deleting_a_clause","historyId":"80d386ea6579b1d3dd7c98b028e33a5e","time":{"start":1791925596458,"stop":1791925596461,"duration":3},"description":"The exact shape the first attempt got wrong: a six-clause\n    \"A exists. ... F exists.\" criteria comes back with `F exists` still in\n    it, folded into the final clause rather than deleted.\n\n    #209 defect 1 folds in the COMBINED case, which no other node covered:\n    a criteria tripping BOTH lexical lints at once is repaired in one\n    `repair_criteria` call, both lint names are recorded in the order they\n    acted, and the result draws no refusal at all -- so a proposal is never\n    accepted on a criteria that merely traded one lint for another. The\n    combined fixture carries TWO bare quantifier clauses on purpose\n    (unit-2 review): the quantifier rewrite bounds one clause per pass, so\n    a single-quantifier fixture cannot tell \"the lint names applied\" --\n    what `SPEC.md` §5.4 and `docs/api.md` promise the event's `lints` field\n    is -- apart from a per-clause operation log.","descriptionHtml":"<p>The exact shape the first attempt got wrong: a six-clause<br />\n&quot;A exists. ... F exists.&quot; criteria comes back with <code>F exists</code> still in<br />\nit, folded into the final clause rather than deleted.</p>\n<pre><code>#209 defect 1 folds in the COMBINED case, which no other node covered:\na criteria tripping BOTH lexical lints at once is repaired in one\n`repair_criteria` call, both lint names are recorded in the order they\nacted, and the result draws no refusal at all -- so a proposal is never\naccepted on a criteria that merely traded one lint for another. The\ncombined fixture carries TWO bare quantifier clauses on purpose\n(unit-2 review): the quantifier rewrite bounds one clause per pass, so\na single-quantifier fixture cannot tell &quot;the lint names applied&quot; --\nwhat `SPEC.md` §5.4 and `docs/api.md` promise the event's `lints` field\nis -- apart from a per-clause operation log.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791925216608,"stop":1791925216609,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1791925216609,"stop":1791925216610,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_home_in_process","time":{"start":1791925596451,"stop":1791925596454,"duration":3},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1791925596451,"stop":1791925596451,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_scrub_notifier_env_in_process","time":{"start":1791925596454,"stop":1791925596456,"duration":2},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_task_record_dir","time":{"start":1791925596454,"stop":1791925596454,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_stub_esca